rk and of course an  unforgettable cameo from bill murray as  himself  so do you have any regrets  garfield maybe with this many laughs  it's no wonder that zombieland  cultivated a fanbase so devoted that it  got a sequel an entire decade after its  release in zombieland double tap  much like the walking dead zombieland  refuses to die  and it's not hard to see why comedy is  this good a rarer than a twinkie in the  apocalypse  looking for a zombie movie to watch for  the whole family the options may be  scarce but paranorman proves her out  there  the second film from leica studios  paranorman is the offbeat story of  norman  a kid who can see ghosts and follows his  quest to save his small town from  puritan zombies and the witch's curse  the project may not be as intense as  your typical zombie flick  but it shouldn't surprise anyone  familiar with leica's infamously creepy  first feature coraline that there's no  shortage of scares here  regardless of age rating the zombies and  ghosts in paranorman aren't just here  for the frights though  they help tell a delightful story about  friendship acceptance and what makes all  of us unique  each frame is lovingly crafted with  leica's impressive stop-motion animation  which lends a signature tactile quality  to everything from a zombie's dangling  jaw to a smear of nail polish  paranorman is a film that's equal parts  chilling and thoughtful  and its overwhelming heart has made it  one of the more critically acclaimed  animated movies  of the 21st century this insightful take  on the genre is perfect for  horror-loving parents who want to get  their children in on the action from a  young age  zombie movies have been used as a means  for providing social commentary since  night of the living dead  a trend that continued into 2020 with  jeff varmedy's blood quantum  in this film as a zombie apocalypse  spreads across north america  the native residents of a first nations  reserve finds themselves strangely  immune fr